<%# The People identity capture (docs/PEOPLE.md §2): the dashboard is about
    the circle — relationships the user chose to tend — not the imported
    roster. It leads only while the circle is empty; after that the circle
    card's own "Add someone" is the one way in, rather than two forms for
    the same thing on one screen (D-person-picker). %>
<%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(
      title: "Who do you want to stay close to?",
      subtitle: "This page is about the relationships you're tending — your full address book stays in the vault."
    ) do %>
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= form_with url: people_circle_path, class: "flex max-w-lg items-center gap-2" do %>
      <%= render Ui::PersonPickerComponent.new(place: :circle, label: "Add to your circle", inline: true,
            placeholder: address_book_size.positive? ? "Search your address book, or type a new name…" : "Name someone…") %>
      <%= submit_tag "Add", class: "btn btn-primary shrink-0" %>
    <% end %>
    <% if address_book_size.zero? %>
      <p class="hint">
        Or <%= link_to "import your address book", new_people_import_path, class: "text-primary-700 hover:underline" %>
        and pick from it here.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
